WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:01.901
-Welcome back.

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:03.067
We are here with Zoe Kravitz,
everybody!

00:00:03.067 --> 00:00:06.467
We're talking about
"The Batman"!

00:00:06.467 --> 00:00:08.667
"The Batman's" out this weekend.

00:00:08.667 --> 00:00:10.901
Fandom is huge.

00:00:10.901 --> 00:00:13.100
Have you seen this
with an audience yet?

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:16.400
-I watched it last night
with an actual audience...

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.067
-You did.
-...at the premiere,

00:00:18.067 --> 00:00:19.968
which is why
I'm so hungover right now.

00:00:19.968 --> 00:00:21.701
[ Laughter ]

00:00:21.701 --> 00:00:24.334
-I mean -- is it --
It must have been so exciting.

00:00:24.334 --> 00:00:25.901
-It's amazing.
I mean, it's definitely

00:00:25.901 --> 00:00:27.734
something you want
to watch on a big screen.

00:00:27.734 --> 00:00:30.100
It's definitely something
you want to watch with people.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.033
But it's a very --
it's an intense film,

00:00:32.033 --> 00:00:34.834
and I think a lot of people walk
in going like, "Whoo, Batman!"

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:36.634
and they leave like,
"Whoa, Batman."

00:00:36.634 --> 00:00:38.501
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:38.501 --> 00:00:40.667
Is that the reaction you're
getting so far from everybody?

00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:42.200
-Yeah, I think people
are surprised

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.467
by how much depth
is in the story.

00:00:44.467 --> 00:00:46.400
I think Matt
just did a really beautiful job

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.934
at grounding the characters
in the world of Gotham.

00:00:48.934 --> 00:00:52.434
-And also, I like what they did.
Because you -- you are Catwoman,

00:00:52.434 --> 00:00:54.467
but you're not actually --

00:00:54.467 --> 00:00:56.734
I mean, you're not actually --
-Yeah, I'm not Catwoman yet.

00:00:56.734 --> 00:00:58.267
-Yes.
-I'm Selina Kyle.

00:00:58.267 --> 00:00:59.601
-Yes.
-Yes.

00:00:59.601 --> 00:01:00.868
-You're not Catwoman yet.
-Yeah.

00:01:00.868 --> 00:01:03.901
-Yeah, but I loved --
Can we say your mask?

00:01:03.901 --> 00:01:05.601
-Yeah. Yeah, yeah.
-Your mask is basically just

00:01:05.601 --> 00:01:07.400
a ski hat or a beanie...
-Yeah.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.701
-...with a hole cut in it.
-Yeah.

00:01:09.701 --> 00:01:11.167
-And you look so cool.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.167 --> 00:01:12.701
And I'm like,
"How does --"

00:01:12.701 --> 00:01:14.334
That's why I lost the audition.

00:01:14.334 --> 00:01:15.901
When I auditioned, I was like,
I did that,

00:01:15.901 --> 00:01:17.434
And they were like,
"Dude, get lost."

00:01:17.434 --> 00:01:19.267
[ Laughter ]
But, honestly, and --

00:01:19.267 --> 00:01:20.534
and it's got little --
you got the cat ear --

00:01:20.534 --> 00:01:22.267
-Very subtle little ears.
Yeah.

00:01:22.267 --> 00:01:24.167
-But I was like, "Dude,
that's a great thing

00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:26.334
'cause it's a mask
for someone who...

00:01:26.334 --> 00:01:28.100
-Who doesn't have the means
to really make it.

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:29.601
-You're not Bruce Wayne.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:01:29.601 --> 00:01:31.200
She's not Bruce Wayne.
-You're not a millionaire, yeah.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:35.067
-And because she's not Catwoman
yet, Matt really wanted to

00:01:35.067 --> 00:01:37.200
kind of have somewhere to go
so we can, you know,

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:38.701
get to the place
where we see the --

00:01:38.701 --> 00:01:41.234
the Catwoman mask eventually.
But this is where it starts.

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:42.467
-Here's what
I liked about it, too,

00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:45.033
'cause I always think of, like,
"Oh, Halloween."

00:01:45.033 --> 00:01:46.501
-Oh, yeah.
Anyone can do it.

00:01:46.501 --> 00:01:47.868
-Anyone can be...
-Buy a beanie.

00:01:47.868 --> 00:01:49.300
-...you for Halloween.
-Yeah.

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:51.734
-Any ski hat you have,
cut a hole in the front,

00:01:51.734 --> 00:01:53.400
and you're Catwoman
for Halloween.

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:55.701
-The only thing about that is,
if no one does it,

00:01:55.701 --> 00:01:58.000
it's more offensive.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.000 --> 00:01:59.267
-No, trust me.

00:01:59.267 --> 00:02:00.467
Trust me,
everyone's gonna do it.

00:02:00.467 --> 00:02:01.634
It's gonna be giant.

00:02:01.634 --> 00:02:03.234
I could already tell, like,
"Oh, my gosh."

00:02:03.234 --> 00:02:04.634
Plus, you look
so cool doing it.

00:02:04.634 --> 00:02:07.334
-Aw, thanks.
-As only you can do.

00:02:07.334 --> 00:02:08.634
Now, how do we set up
"The Batman"

00:02:08.634 --> 00:02:10.834
for anyone who just --
you're going in cold turkey?

00:02:10.834 --> 00:02:14.834
-Oh, man. Okay.
So, this is a detective story.

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:16.634
We're in year two
of Batman being Batman,

00:02:16.634 --> 00:02:18.300
so it's not quite
an origin story,

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:20.234
but it's still the beginning.
Gotham is still --

00:02:20.234 --> 00:02:22.534
-So the public doesn't really
know who is the Batman?

00:02:22.534 --> 00:02:24.434
-Yeah, and the cops are like,
"Who is this guy?"

00:02:24.434 --> 00:02:25.968
-"Do we trust this guy?"
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:25.968 --> 00:02:29.300
And there's a serial killer
in Gotham and he kind of

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:31.267
has to --
you know, he follows the --

00:02:31.267 --> 00:02:33.534
the clues and figures out
who's -- what's going on.

00:02:33.534 --> 00:02:37.234
And the clues lead him to
a nightclub where I work.

00:02:37.234 --> 00:02:41.300
-Yeah.
Man, it's action, it's romance.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:43.601
It's --
There's jokes in there.

00:02:43.601 --> 00:02:45.801
It's just --
It's just great music.

00:02:45.801 --> 00:02:47.200
It's just --
-The music's amazing.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:49.234
-It's dark, it's cool.
It's awesome.

00:02:49.234 --> 00:02:50.801
It's just --
You guys are gonna love it.

00:02:50.801 --> 00:02:52.734
I want to show everyone a clip.
Here's Zoe Kravitz

00:02:52.734 --> 00:02:54.968
and Robert Pattinson
in "The Batman."

00:02:54.968 --> 00:02:56.467
Take a look.

00:02:56.467 --> 00:03:00.434
[ Tumbler clicking, loud thunk ]

00:03:00.434 --> 00:03:02.434
-You're pretty good at that.

00:03:02.434 --> 00:03:10.133
♪♪

00:03:10.133 --> 00:03:17.834
♪♪

00:03:17.834 --> 00:03:25.567
♪♪

00:03:25.567 --> 00:03:33.267
♪♪

00:03:33.267 --> 00:03:36.601
-Hey, gimme that.

00:03:36.601 --> 00:03:38.868
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Whoo!

00:03:38.868 --> 00:03:40.400
Zoe Kravitz, everybody!

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:43.968
"The Batman" is in theaters
and IMAX this Friday.

